{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And the lambs Jacob separated.</b> Those born ringed and spotted he separated and set apart for himself, and made them a flock unto themselves alone. And he led that ringed flock in front of the sheep, and the faces of the sheep walking behind them gazed at them. And this is what is said, ״וַיָּשֶׂם פְּנֵי הַצֹּאן אֶל עָקֹד״ — that the faces of the sheep were toward the ringed ones, and toward every brown he found in Laban's flock." "<b>And he set himself flocks.</b> As I have explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:23.024383048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}